{"document_id":"cir-glycolic-acid-safety-assessment-v1","title":"Glycolic Acid — CIR (AHA) safety-assessment factual card","source":"Cosmetic Ingredient Review (CIR)","source_family":"CIR","source_url":"https://www.cir-safety.org/sites/default/files/ahas.pdf","published_year":1998,"document_type":"regulatory-safety-provenance-card","evidence_tier":"regulatory-safety-provenance","chunk_text":"Paraphrased CIR conclusion: in the Safety Assessment of Alpha Hydroxy Acids the CIR Expert Panel concluded that Glycolic Acid (and Lactic Acid), their common salts and simple esters, are safe for use in cosmetic products at concentrations of 10% or less, at a final formulation pH of 3.5 or greater, when formulated to avoid increasing sun sensitivity (or with directions for daily sun protection). Higher limits apply only to professional/salon use. Paraphrased factual summary; no verbatim CIR text is stored.","source_locator":"Safety Assessment of Alpha Hydroxy Acids as Used in Cosmetics (CIR).","citation_text":"Cosmetic Ingredient Review. Safety Assessment of Alpha Hydroxy Acids (Glycolic and Lactic Acid) as Used in Cosmetics.","claim_category":"ingredient-regulatory-safety-context","clinical_review_status":"pending: qualified review must reconfirm against source before activation.","reuse_rights_status":"attribution_only","reuse_rights_basis":"Factual paraphrase with attribution and source link; protected expression not reproduced.","verification_status":"verified_paraphrase","verified_by":"web-search-assisted draft — reviewer must reconfirm against source","verified_at":"2026-07-27","product_specific":false,"attribution_required":true,"routine_selection_allowed":false,"ingredient_ids":["glycolic-acid"],"ingredient_names":["Glycolic Acid"],"inci_names":["Glycolic Acid"]}
{"document_id":"cir-lactic-acid-safety-assessment-v1","title":"Lactic Acid — CIR (AHA) safety-assessment factual card","source":"Cosmetic Ingredient Review (CIR)","source_family":"CIR","source_url":"https://www.cir-safety.org/sites/default/files/ahas.pdf","published_year":1998,"document_type":"regulatory-safety-provenance-card","evidence_tier":"regulatory-safety-provenance","chunk_text":"Paraphrased CIR conclusion: in the Safety Assessment of Alpha Hydroxy Acids the CIR Expert Panel concluded that Lactic Acid (and Glycolic Acid), their common salts and simple esters, are safe for use in cosmetic products at concentrations of 10% or less, at a final formulation pH of 3.5 or greater, when formulated to avoid increasing sun sensitivity (or with directions for daily sun protection). The Panel noted AHAs can increase UV sensitivity. Paraphrased factual summary; no verbatim CIR text is stored.","source_locator":"Safety Assessment of Alpha Hydroxy Acids as Used in Cosmetics (CIR).","citation_text":"Cosmetic Ingredient Review. Safety Assessment of Alpha Hydroxy Acids (Glycolic and Lactic Acid) as Used in Cosmetics.","claim_category":"ingredient-regulatory-safety-context","clinical_review_status":"pending: qualified review must reconfirm against source before activation.","reuse_rights_status":"attribution_only","reuse_rights_basis":"Factual paraphrase with attribution and source link; protected expression not reproduced.","verification_status":"verified_paraphrase","verified_by":"web-search-assisted draft — reviewer must reconfirm against source","verified_at":"2026-07-27","product_specific":false,"attribution_required":true,"routine_selection_allowed":false,"ingredient_ids":["lactic-acid"],"ingredient_names":["Lactic Acid"],"inci_names":["Lactic Acid"]}
{"document_id":"cir-dimethicone-safety-assessment-v1","title":"Dimethicone — CIR safety-assessment factual card","source":"Cosmetic Ingredient Review (CIR)","source_family":"CIR","source_url":"https://www.cir-safety.org/sites/default/files/methic122020revTAR.pdf","published_year":2020,"document_type":"regulatory-safety-provenance-card","evidence_tier":"regulatory-safety-provenance","chunk_text":"Paraphrased CIR conclusion: in the amended Safety Assessment covering Dimethicone and related methicone/dimethicone ingredients, the CIR Expert Panel concluded these ingredients are safe in the present practices of use and concentration. These are large polymers not expected to penetrate skin. Paraphrased factual summary; no verbatim CIR text is stored.","source_locator":"Amended Safety Assessment of Dimethicone, Methicone, and related ingredients (CIR).","citation_text":"Cosmetic Ingredient Review. Amended Safety Assessment of Dimethicone, Methicone, and Related Ingredients as Used in Cosmetics.","claim_category":"ingredient-regulatory-safety-context","clinical_review_status":"pending: qualified review must reconfirm against source before activation.","reuse_rights_status":"attribution_only","reuse_rights_basis":"Factual paraphrase with attribution and source link; protected expression not reproduced.","verification_status":"verified_paraphrase","verified_by":"web-search-assisted draft — reviewer must reconfirm against source","verified_at":"2026-07-27","product_specific":false,"attribution_required":true,"routine_selection_allowed":false,"ingredient_ids":["dimethicone"],"ingredient_names":["Dimethicone"],"inci_names":["Dimethicone"]}
{"document_id":"cir-petrolatum-deferred-fda-v1","title":"Petrolatum — CIR deferral / FDA regulatory factual card","source":"Cosmetic Ingredient Review (CIR)","source_family":"CIR","source_url":"https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredient/petrolatum/","published_year":"","document_type":"regulatory-safety-provenance-card","evidence_tier":"regulatory-safety-provenance","chunk_text":"Paraphrased factual status: CIR deferred an independent safety assessment of Petrolatum because it is regulated by the US FDA (Petrolatum is an FDA OTC skin-protectant active). Cosmetic-grade petrolatum is highly refined with limits on polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons. This card records a regulatory deferral, not an independent CIR 'safe as used' conclusion. Paraphrased factual summary; no verbatim text is stored.","source_locator":"CIR deferral to FDA; FDA OTC skin-protectant monograph status.","citation_text":"Cosmetic Ingredient Review deferral to FDA; FDA OTC skin-protectant drug status for Petrolatum.","claim_category":"ingredient-regulatory-safety-context","clinical_review_status":"pending: qualified review must reconfirm regulatory status before activation.","reuse_rights_status":"attribution_only","reuse_rights_basis":"Factual paraphrase with attribution and source link; protected expression not reproduced.","verification_status":"verified_paraphrase","verified_by":"web-search-assisted draft — deferral status; reviewer to confirm FDA monograph","verified_at":"2026-07-27","product_specific":false,"attribution_required":true,"routine_selection_allowed":false,"ingredient_ids":["petrolatum"],"ingredient_names":["Petrolatum"],"inci_names":["Petrolatum"]}
